<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lübeck</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lubeck is a port city on the Baltic coast of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> and was the leading city of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hanseatic-league">Hanseatic League</a>. As a free imperial city of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire</a>, it dominated much of the medieval Baltic and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-sea">North Sea</a> trade. Its prosperity illustrates the commercial role of the empire's self-governing cities.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lubeck.jpg" alt="Lübeck" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Oleg Dejan · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:L%C3%BCbeck_-_panoramio.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
